  "question": {
    "text": "The electric field in a space <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mover><mi>E</mi><mo>→</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>-</mo><mn>5</mn><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">k</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi><mo>&nbsp;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>. What is the potential difference <math><msub><mrow><mi>V</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>B</mi></mrow></msub><mo>-</mo><msub><mrow><mi>V</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>A</mi></mrow></msub></math> between points <math><mi>A</mi></math> and <math><mi>B</mi></math>? The coordinates of <math><mi>A</mi></math> and <math><mi>B</mi></math> are <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&nbsp;</mi><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&nbsp;</mi><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&nbsp;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math> and <math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>10</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>&nbsp;</mi><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>&nbsp;</mi><mn>0</mn></mrow></mfenced><mi>&nbsp;</mi><mi>m</mi></math>, respectively."
